<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- ========================================================================
       RSW_DW_Power — the droid power need. Backs
       RimMandrake.StarWars.Droidworks.Need_Power
       (Source/Droidworks/Need_Power.cs). Falls at the race's
       DroidworksExtension.powerFallPerDay; at 0.02 the C# applies RSW_DW_PoweredDown
       via NeedInterval (state 3 — see HediffDefs_Droidworks.xml). Fields match a
       vanilla NeedDef shape 1:1 (RimWorld's own Chemical_* needs), not guessed.

       🔴 FIXED 2026-09-02 (FOUNDRY, opus code review): needClass was the bare
       "Droidworks.Need_Power" — GenTypes.GetTypeInAnyAssembly does EXACT
       matching only, never a namespace-suffix match, so this resolved to null
       and every droid silently failed AddNeed (caught, logged, swallowed) —
       no droid ever had this need. The whole power-exhaustion route into
       RSW_DW_PoweredDown, both charger comps, and Recipe_RebootDroid's charge
       restore were all dead as a result. This was the actual root cause
       DROIDWORKS_POWEREDDOWN_NOT_WIRED_1 was chasing.

       🔴 THAT FIX UNMASKED A SEPARATE, WORSE BUG, fixed the same session
       (re-review pass): this def has NO gating field — no minIntelligence,
       hediffRequiredAny, colonistsOnly, requiredComps. Verified against
       Pawn_NeedsTracker.ShouldHaveNeed: with every gate at its default, the
       need reaches EVERY pawn in the game, not just droids — human,
       animal, mechanoid alike. Since only droid race ThingDefs carry
       Recipe_RebootDroid, every other pawn drains to 0 in ~1.5 in-game
       days and is permanently, irrecoverably downed. Fixed with a Harmony
       postfix, Patch_ShouldHaveNeed_Power.cs, narrowing this need to
       FleshType == RSW_DW_FleshType_Droid — the NeedDef itself still has
       no native gate, the C# patch is the actual gate.
  ======================================================================== -->
  <NeedDef>
    <defName>RSW_DW_Power</defName>
    <needClass>RimMandrake.StarWars.Droidworks.Need_Power</needClass>
    <label>power</label>
    <description>Stored charge. A droid whose power runs out shuts down until someone reboots it.</description>
    <showOnNeedList>true</showOnNeedList>
    <major>false</major>
  </NeedDef>

</Defs>
